# 📚 Intelligent Reading Comprehension & Quiz Generation System

**Course:** Artificial Intelligence — BS (CS) Spring 2026  
**Institution:** NUCES FAST, Islamabad Campus

---

## 🎯 Project Overview

An AI-powered system that:

1. Accepts a reading passage as input
2. Generates a multiple-choice question (template-based + ML-ranked)
3. Produces 4 options (1 correct + 3 ML-generated distractors)
4. Verifies user answers (Logistic Regression + SVM ensemble)
5. Provides graduated hints (extractive + ML-scored)
6. Displays analytics via a Streamlit dashboard

### Models

| Model   | Task                         | Approach                                |
| ------- | ---------------------------- | --------------------------------------- |
| Model A | Answer Verification          | LR + SVM + K-Means + Soft-Vote Ensemble |
| Model B | Distractor & Hint Generation | LR Ranker + Extractive Scorer           |

---

## 🗂️ Project Structure

```
race_rc_project/
├── data/
│   ├── raw/            ← Place train.csv / val.csv / test.csv here (RACE dataset)
│   └── processed/      ← Auto-generated artefacts
├── models/
│   ├── model_a/traditional/
│   └── model_b/traditional/
├── src/
│   ├── preprocessing.py
│   ├── model_a_train.py
│   ├── model_b_train.py
│   ├── inference.py
│   └── evaluate.py
├── ui/
│   └── app.py
├── notebooks/
│   └── EDA.ipynb
├── requirements.txt
└── README.md
```

---

## ⚙️ Setup Instructions

### 1. Install dependencies

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

### 2. Download RACE Dataset

Download from Kaggle: https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/ankitdhiman7/race-dataset  
Place the training CSV in `C:\Users\mosaq\Desktop\AI Proj\race_rc_project\data\raw\` (e.g. `train.csv`, as used by `preprocessing.load_data()`).  
The pipeline will split it into 80/10/10 automatically.

### 3. Run Preprocessing

```bash
cd src
python preprocessing.py
```

Optional: maximize cosine-similarity features (larger vocab + ngrams):

```bash
TFIDF_MAX_FEATURES=50000 TFIDF_MIN_DF=1 TFIDF_NGRAM_MAX=2 \
OHE_MAX_FEATURES=50000 OHE_MIN_DF=1 OHE_NGRAM_MAX=2 \
python preprocessing.py
```

### 4. Train Model A

```bash
python model_a_train.py
```

Metrics are automatically exported to `data/processed/reports/model_a_*.csv` files.

### 5. Train Model B

```bash
python model_b_train.py
```

Metrics are automatically exported to `data/processed/reports/model_b_metrics.csv`.

### 6. Evaluate

```bash
python evaluate.py
```

### 7. Launch Streamlit UI

```bash
cd ..
streamlit run ui/app.py
```

> **Note:** The UI works in demo mode even without trained models, using rule-based inference.

---

## 📊 Evaluation Metrics

- BLEU Score
- ROUGE Score (ROUGE-1 / ROUGE-2 / ROUGE-L)
- METEOR Score

---

## 🔬 Dataset

RACE (ReAding Comprehension from Examinations) — Lai et al., EMNLP 2017  
~28,000 passages · ~100,000 questions · Source: Chinese school English exams

---

## ⚠️ Ethical Notice

Generated questions are AI-produced and must not be used in real exam settings without human review. The system clearly marks all outputs as AI-generated.

